Package: baseline-drive-setup
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, polkitd, pkexec, qemu-system-x86
Maintainer: Cliff Thelin <cliffthelin@gmail.com>
Description: BaselineOS drive setup GUI
 A GTK4 application for preparing a new bootable BaselineOS/Proxmox
 drive. Privileged operations run through PolicyKit (pkexec), the
 standard OS authentication mechanism used by GNOME/KDE system tools -
 no custom sudo rules, no NOPASSWD grants. The privileged helper this
 app authorizes is installed read-only, root-owned, by this package
 (standard dpkg file-permission handling, the same mechanism that gives
 /usr/bin/sudo and /usr/bin/pkexec themselves their special permissions).
